.TH ALARMQT 1 "October 2026" "alarmqt" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
alarmqt \- keyboard-friendly system-tray alarms and reminders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B alarmqt
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIALARM\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B alarmqt
is a small Qt6 system-tray alarm application for Linux.
It accepts relative times (for example
.Qq in 5m )
and absolute times (for example
.Qq at 15:10 ),
optionally with a short human-readable note.
Alarms keep notifying (dialog, tray message, and sound) until they are
acknowledged or snoozed.
.PP
Only one instance runs at a time.
A second invocation forwards the command line to the running process
(raise the window, add an alarm, quit, and so on).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the full version string and exit.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quit
Quit the running instance.
If none is running, exit successfully without starting the GUI.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List alarms.
If no instance is running, print the list and exit without starting the GUI.
If an instance is running, the request is forwarded (the second process does
not print the list).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-raise
Raise the existing main window.
.SH ALARM EXPRESSIONS
.SS Relative
.BR in\ 5m ,
.BR in\ 2h30m ,
.BR in\ 1d ,
.BR 5m ,
.BR 30s
.SS Absolute
.BR at\ 15:10 ,
.BR at\ 2026\-10\-03\ 09:00 ,
.BR 15:10
(next occurrence if that clock time has already passed today)
.SS Notes
Text after the time expression becomes the alarm label; the command column
keeps only the time part:
.PP
.RS
.B in 5m kitchen
.br
.B in 5m, tea
.br
.B at 15:10 standup
.RE
.PP
Parentheses and quotes still work:
.BR "in 5m (kitchen)" ,
.BR "in 5m \(dqtea\(dq" .
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
Focus the add line.
.TP
.B Enter
Add an alarm from the input line (main window).
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
Edit the selected alarm.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Restart the selected alarm (re-evaluate its command from now).
.TP
.B Delete / Ctrl+D
Remove the selected alarm(s).
.TP
.B Esc
Hide the main window to the tray; in the notification dialog, snooze 5 minutes.
.TP
.B Enter / Space
Acknowledge in the notification dialog.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Grumbel/alarmqt/alarms.json
Typical path for the JSON alarm store on Linux
(Qt AppDataLocation with organization
.B Grumbel
and application
.BR alarmqt ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Could not parse an alarm expression given on the command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start or raise the app:
.RS
.B alarmqt
.RE
.TP
Add a relative alarm with a note:
.RS
.B alarmqt \(dqin 5m kitchen\(dq
.RE
.TP
Add an absolute alarm:
.RS
.B alarmqt \(dqat 15:10\(dq
.RE
.TP
List alarms without opening the GUI (when idle):
.RS
.B alarmqt \-\-list
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/Grumbel/alarmqt
.UE
